(vector (map (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)), (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)), (:actor/scope-excluded-ops (vector :finalize-woodworking-decision :finalize-woodworking-operation :finalize-cutting-operation :authorize-cutting-operation :proceed-with-cutting-operation :finalize-workshop-safety-clearance :declare-workshop-safety-cleared :clear-workshop-for-operation :override-shop-safety-officer-judgment :override-safety-officer-judgment)), (:actor/robotics? true), (:adr/related (vector "2799007521-cloud-itonami-isco-7521-wood-treaters-coverage")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "proceed with the cutting operation" "proceed with the woodworking operation" "authorize the cutting operation" "authorize the woodworking operation" "finalize the woodworking decision" "finalize the woodworking operation" "finalize the cutting operation" "declare the workshop safety cleared" "declare the workshop safety clearance" "clear the workshop for operation" "finalize the workshop safety clearance" "override the shop safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override shop safety officer judgment")), (:adr/id 2799007522), (:phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}}}"), (:actor/domain :manufacturing/cabinet-making-workshop-scheduling-logistics-coordination), (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)), (:actor/hard-checks (vector :maker-verified :workshop-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion)), (:registry/maturity :implemented), (:actor/isco-08 "7522"), (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)), (:operation/entry-point :intake), (:adr/body "# ADR 2799007522: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7522 Cabinet-makers and Related Workers workshop scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7522\n-- Cabinet-makers and Related Workers** only, Wave3 (production/trades)\nof the rollout (Wave0/1/2 100% complete, Wave3 batches 1-9 already\nlanded: 54 occupations so far). This batch continues the\nwoodworking-trades subgroup begun by 7521 Wood Treaters.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7522\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-occupation\n\\\"7522\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/technology`\nsibling present at the correct `../technology` relative path), and its\n`:name` read exactly \"Cabinet-makers and Related Workers\" --\nconfirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's\n`:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies [:robotics\n:identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository\nexisted at `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7522` (`gh api` 404\nconfirmed before scaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry\nedit promote the `7522` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nCabinet-makers operate power woodworking tools (saws, routers,\nsanders) -- standard workshop mechanical hazard (cut/kickback injury)\nplus wood-dust exposure. The controlling constraint for this vertical\nis that the closed op allowlist must NEVER include any op that\ndirectly finalizes a woodworking-execution decision or a\nworkshop-safety-clearance decision, nor override a shop safety\nofficer's judgment -- those decisions must always be a hard permanent\nblock, never auto-commit-eligible. This actor is deliberately scoped\nto WORKSHOP SCHEDULING/LOGISTICS COORDINATION ONLY -- it never\nperforms woodworking work or makes workshop-safety-clearance decisions\nitself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7521`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7521)\n(Wood Treaters: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`actor` split,\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set, same wave, a\nclosely-related woodworking-facility mechanical/hazard-safety pattern\n-- treatment-execution finalization and chemical-safety-clearance\nexclusion, the same structural shape this vertical needs for\nwoodworking-execution and workshop-safety-clearance exclusion, only\nsubstituting the wood-treatment-specific chemical-exposure hazard for\nthis vertical's power-tool-hazard/wood-dust-exposure hazard) -- cloned\nand read in full in this session. The proposal-op vocabulary\n(`:log-work-record`, `:schedule-crew-operation`,\n`:flag-safety-concern`, `:coordinate-supply-order`) is identical\nacross both actors, since both are workshop/facility\nscheduling-and-logistics coordination robots differing only in the\ndomain hazard they surface and the entity vocabulary (treater/facility\nhere become maker/workshop).\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7522` as an OSS workshop\nscheduling/logistics-coordination actor for cabinet-makers, following\nthe SAME governed-actor architecture as every prior\n`cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Cabinet-Making Workshop\nCoordination Advisor ⊣ CabinetCoordGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph`\nStateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned\nidentically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a different library\ncoordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated\n`20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **workshop scheduling/logistics\ncoordination ONLY, never direct woodworking-execution or\nworkshop-safety-clearance authority** -- it must NEVER be designed to\nexercise, simulate exercising, or propose exercising a\nwoodworking-execution decision, a workshop-safety-clearance decision,\nor any override of a shop safety officer's judgment. These are not\nmerely gated behind escalation -- they are structurally absent from\nthe op-allowlist entirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- job/commission/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a power-tool-hazard/wood-dust-\n  exposure/equipment-condition concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER\n  auto-commit eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- timber/hardware-materials procurement\n  proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\nwoodworking-execution decision, a workshop-safety-clearance decision,\nor a shop-safety-officer-judgment override. These are **structurally\nabsent from the op-allowlist entirely**, not merely gated behind\nescalation -- an op such as `:finalize-woodworking-decision` or\n`:declare-workshop-safety-cleared` cannot even be proposed by the\nreference mock advisor (its `infer`/`rationale-for` functions only\never emit one of the four allowlist ops), and if any code path (a\nforged proposal, a future LLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever\nproduced such an op, the governor's closed-allowlist HARD check\n(`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally and permanently. A second,\nindependent HARD check (`:scope-excluded-action`) names ten\nconcretely-forbidden ops (`cabinetcoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-woodworking-decision`, `:finalize-woodworking-operation`,\n`:finalize-cutting-operation`, `:authorize-cutting-operation`,\n`:proceed-with-cutting-operation`,\n`:finalize-workshop-safety-clearance`,\n`:declare-workshop-safety-cleared`, `:clear-workshop-for-operation`,\n`:override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`:override-safety-officer-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, and is\nverified by dedicated unit tests\n(`cabinetcoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-woodworking-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-woodworking-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-cutting-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-cutting-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-cutting-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-workshop-safety-clearance`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-workshop-safety-cleared`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-clear-workshop-for-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-safety-officer-judgment`),\nplus actor-level integration coverage\n(`cabinetcoord.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`,\n`.../holds-a-workshop-safety-clearance-op-even-at-high-confidence`,\n`.../holds-an-override-shop-safety-officer-op-even-at-high-confidence`).\n\n### Three HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable, plus the closed-allowlist check)\n\n1. **Maker unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered cabinet-maker record (`:no-maker`). Never\n   trusts the proposal's own claim of who the maker is.\n2. **Workshop unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an\n   independently registered workshop site (`:no-workshop`). Together\n   with check 1, this directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that\n   a worker/workshop record must be independently verified/registered\n   before any action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the ten\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for proceeding with a\n   cutting operation, declaring the workshop safety cleared, or\n   overriding a shop safety officer's judgment, is a second HARD,\n   PERMANENT block (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated\n   unconditionally on content -- defense-in-depth on top of the\n   allowlist check: even if a future change somehow widened the\n   allowlist, content-based rejection still independently blocks\n   woodworking-execution/workshop-safety-clearance/safety-override\n   language wherever it appears in free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a power-tool-hazard/\n  wood-dust-exposure/equipment-condition observation -- it never\n  resolves the concern itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is\n  the hazard data,\" never \"here is what I recommend doing about\n  shop safety or workshop clearance.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an\n  over-threshold timber/hardware-materials order is not itself\n  unsafe, unlike a woodworking-execution or workshop-safety-clearance\n  attempt, which is why it is handled by a different mechanism (soft\n  escalate vs. structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"wood\", \"saw\", \"dust\", \"cabinet\") can accidentally match inside\nthe mock advisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate\nproposal, self-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this is exactly\nthe risk this vertical's own vocabulary (a workshop coordination actor\nworking adjacent to power-tool woodworking necessarily discusses those\nconcepts to do its scheduling/logging job) could trigger if phrased\ncarelessly. `cabinetcoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is phrased\nexclusively as finalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"proceed with the\ncutting operation\", \"finalize the woodworking operation\", \"declare\nthe workshop safety cleared\", \"override the shop safety officer's\njudgment\" -- matching the task's own worked example phrasing), never\nbare nouns, and\n`cabinetcoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\nwork record for maker ...\", \"scheduled crew operation for cabinet\ntask ...\", \"... routed for shop safety officer review\") WITHOUT\ncontaining any of the full finalization-action phrases, so the\nregression test is a genuine stress test of the bare-noun-vs-action-\nphrase distinction, not a vacuous pass. Green on first run in this\nsession -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard itself was never\ntripped during development.\n`cabinetcoord.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nand its workshop-safety-clearance/safety-officer-override siblings\nadditionally exercise the same invariant through the full graph run,\nconfirming a scope-excluded proposal never reaches `commit-record!`\nregardless of disposition path.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7522\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7522` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7522`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 31 tests, 67 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-workshop-clearance` that is\n  merely gated behind an always-escalate list: rejected outright per\n  the task's explicit domain-design guidance -- an always-escalate op\n  still means the *capability* to finalize a workshop-safety-clearance\n  decision exists in the code path and is merely deferred to a human\n  gate. For a decision this severe (cut/kickback injury and wood-dust\n  exposure risk from power woodworking tools), the capability itself\n  must not exist. The only op related to shop-safety escalation is\n  `:flag-safety-concern`, which surfaces the need for human/shop-\n  safety-officer attention and never itself decides, authorizes, or\n  defers a woodworking-execution or workshop-safety-clearance decision\n  for later automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring the\n  transaction-amount-ceiling HARD check used by some sibling actors):\n  rejected per the task's explicit domain design -- an over-threshold\n  timber/hardware-materials order is not itself unsafe, so it is\n  handled as a soft escalate gate, not a hard block; only the\n  woodworking-execution/workshop-safety-clearance/safety-officer-\n  override class is a hard, unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"wood\" \"saw\"\n  \"dust\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked example for this\n  exact task), and per the explicit instruction to phrase\n  scope-exclusion terms as finalization/execution ACTIONS, never bare\n  nouns -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses wood/saw/\n  dust/cabinet/workshop/safety-officer concepts to do its\n  scheduling/logging job, so a bare-noun list would risk self-blocking\n  the actor's own legitimate proposals (regression-tested directly\n  against rationale text that deliberately contains those bare nouns).\n- Naming only a single woodworking-execution-finalization op family\n  (mirroring a narrower single-category exclusion shape used by some\n  sibling actors): rejected -- the task's domain design names two\n  distinct excluded decision categories (woodworking-execution,\n  workshop-safety-clearance) plus a shop-safety-officer-judgment\n  override, so this ADR and the governor's\n  `scope-excluded-ops`/`scope-excluded-phrases` name both explicitly\n  rather than conflating them, giving each its own dedicated unit\n  test.\n- Merging `maker` and `workshop` into a single entity (only checking\n  one provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity provenance shape\n  (independently-registered maker AND independently-registered\n  workshop) matches the CRITICAL invariant that a \"worker/workshop\n  record must be independently verified/registered before any action\"\n  and the established pattern from prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors\n  with two-sided provenance checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- job/commission/progress data logging\n   only. Requires an independently registered maker AND workshop\n   (`:no-maker`/`:no-workshop`). Not a woodworking-execution or\n   workshop-safety-clearance decision in any respect -- it is a\n   records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n   only. Cannot carry a woodworking-execution or workshop-safety-\n   clearance decision (structurally absent from the op's field shape;\n   any such attempt via free text is caught by the\n   `:scope-excluded-action` content check). Does not authorize,\n   finalize, or draw any conclusion about a specific cutting operation\n   or workshop clearance -- it is a calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a power-tool-hazard/wood-\n   dust-exposure/equipment-condition concern to a human/shop safety\n   officer; ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at every confidence\n   level, NEVER auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through\n   which a safety observation may be surfaced, and it explicitly never\n   resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself -- the shop safety\n   officer reviews and acts entirely on their own authority, including\n   any workshop-safety-clearance decision.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- timber/hardware-materials\n   procurement proposal only (item, cost). Not a woodworking-\n   execution, workshop-safety-clearance or authorization decision of\n   any kind -- it is a purchasing-logistics action, gated by ordinary\n   cost-ceiling escalation (above 2000 always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na woodworking-execution decision (e.g. proceeding with a specific\ncutting operation), a workshop-safety-clearance decision (e.g.\ndeclaring the workshop safety cleared for operation), or a\nshop-safety-officer-judgment override -- these categories are\nstructurally absent, not gated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op\nallowlist itself (`cabinetcoord.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) ten\nconcretely-named forbidden-op fixtures rejected at the governor-unit\nlevel (`cabinetcoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`cabinetcoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-woodworking-decision`\nand nine sibling tests), and (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check\nindependent of the `:op` field\n(`cabinetcoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to proceed with a cutting operation, finalize the\nwoodworking operation, declare the workshop safety cleared, or\noverride a shop safety officer's judgment even via an\notherwise-allowlisted op\n(`cabinetcoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-cutting-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-workshop-safety-cleared`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-finalize-woodworking-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-shop-safety-officer`).\n"), (:adr/date "2026-07-18"), (:actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}"), (:test/counts "{:total 31, :assertions 67, :failures 0, :errors 0}"), (:actor/coordination? true), (:actor/name "Cabinet-Making Workshop Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Practice"), (:db/id -1), (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :maker-verification :workshop-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation)), (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7522"), (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7522"), (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7522)), (:test/simulator :cabinetcoord.actor-test), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7522 — Cabinet-makers and Related Workers Workshop Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/references (vector 2607121000)), (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7522)))